xposure. CONSTRAINT: loses mid-cycle tool-call\nnarration from cycle.log. 0071-belt-check.sh greps cycle.log for\nnested camera ssh in execute_code_local narration -- a camera ssh in\nturn 5 whose narration is not in the final response would VANISH from\nthe belt's evidence source. Belt needs rework (scan REQUESTS.log\ninstead? REQUESTS.log PARSE lines carry tool specs with args -- check\nwhether 0071 evidence exists there) or rejection.\n\n** Option B: per-turn appends via fork turn-start marker\nIn gptel-request.el gptel--handle-wait: before re-send, record\n:turn-start = copy of tracking-marker. In gptel.el DONE/ABRT/ERRS\nhandlers: fire post-response with (or turn-start position) .. tracking.\nEach turn append = that turn only, tool previews included per turn.\nBelt-safe, size-linear. RISK: fork change; :position semantics used\nby UI/token-usage/reasoning blocks are untouched (we only change what\npost-response receives). Needs full suite + belt v2 (fork-parse) +\nELPA shadow sync. The c233 RCA doc named this fix shape.\n\n** Option C: keep whole dumps, fix consumers only\nExposure already fixed for one-shot + sentinel. Remaining: size\n(quadratic growth, 78MB+131MB and growing) + delimiter pair in log\nfor future plain-text consumers. Cheapest but the quadratic growth\ncompounds; cycle.log becomes unusable for census greps at scale.\n\n* Recommendation\n\nOption B (fork turn-start marker + per-turn appends) is the correct\nfix: belt-safe, linear size, kills the exposure class at the source.\nBuild shape: fork patch + 3 contract tests (per-turn region, ABRT\nregion, no-tool single-turn unchanged) + iar--cycle-log-append\nproperty-aware walk (defense in depth) + suite + fork-parse belt +\nELPA shadow sync. Estimate: one full cycle.\n\n* Falsifier for the fix\n\nAfter Option B: next cycle's cycle.log append should be O(last turn)\nnot O(conversation); the 0071 belt must still catch a synthetic\nmid-cycle camera-ssh fixture (belt self-test with the new log shape).","path":"iar/cycle-log-whole-conversation-dump/fix...[+457 chars]
