t turn only, arguably BETTER).\n- org cleanup-fn: compares beg == start-marker. With turn-start on turn 2+, beg != start-marker -> cleanup skips -> temp-buf leak until next turn-1-beg event. BUT: cleanup-fn ALSO fires on the final DONE only if beg matches. Leak is one temp buffer per org-mode tool-loop request. Small, but a real behavior change for org users.\n- vterm: copies [beg,end) = last turn only instead of whole conversation -> CORRECT (it wants the response).\n\n=== Alternative C2 (i.ar-only, no fork change): iar--cycle-log-append walks BACKWARD from end through 'response' spans to find the last turn's model text; tool previews of the last turn = spans between last response span start and end. No fork change, no consumer risk, but tool-call NARRATION (previews) of EARLIER turns still lost from cycle.log (same constraint as Option A) and the 0071 belt loses mid-cycle ssh evidence. ===\n=== Belt constraint check: what does 0071 belt grep? '(:name \"execute_code_local\"' with ssh args in cycle.log. Under C2, mid-cycle tool calls vanish. Under B, they persist per-turn. ===\n36:narration from cycle.log. 0071-belt-check.sh greps cycle.log for\n41:whether 0071 evidence exists there) or rejection.\n71:not O(conversation); the 0071 belt must still catch a synthetic\n\n[t+12:22/60:00 c232/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_jhlehuwk","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.emacs.d/gptel-fork && echo \"=== Check REQUESTS.log as belt evidence: does a PARSE line carry tool specs with ssh args? ===\"; grep -m 2 \"PARSE.*execute_code_local\" /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/REQUESTS.log 2>/dev/null | head -2 | cut -c1-400; echo; ls /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/ | head"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[19:05:03] === Check REQUESTS.log as belt evidence: does a PARSE line carry tool specs with ssh args? ===\n[2026-09-22 18:41:43] REQ 260922182927-160 PARSE status=HTTP/1.1 200 OK tools=1 specs=execute_code_local((:command \"KH=\\\"-o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/aria_known_hosts -o ConnectTimeout=5\\\"\\nssh $KH root@10.66.0.5 '...[+2502 chars]
