[2026-09-22 19:06:17] REQ 260922185238-245 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T19:06:16.965909417Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_2wdjwx4b","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar/emacs.d/init.d/agent \u0026\u0026 echo \"=== output-runaway-p: 20 identical lines in the WHOLE conversation. A normal 100-turn cycle with a repeated template line 20+ times across turns would false-positive TODAY... but wait, has it ever fired wrongly? The falsifier data: c80's false positive was a legit synthesis turn. Hmm, but the guard fires only when the post-response handler runs the runaway check -- and today's region = whole conversation. So ANY line appearing 20x across the whole conversation trips it. Why hasn't this fire constantly? Because iar--cycle-response-text excludes tool spans; model text lines rarely repeat 20x verbatim... but 'I' or short lines might. Actually the deepseek fires were real loops. This is a real false-positive risk TODAY that Option B fixes. ===\"; echo \"=== Now let me also check iar--cycle-terminal-echo-p's \u003c20-char text check under whole-conversation regions: today the region text is huge, so the echo close NEVER fires from the DONE branch (dead code, documented). Under B it could fire... but the FSM never reaches DONE on tool-call turns, so still dead. Fine. ===\"; echo \"=== SUMMARY OF THE CYCLE'S VERIFICATION: c236's mechanism claim CONFIRMED against the artifact at every link: ===\"; echo \"1. :position set once at request setup (gptel-request.el:2262), never advanced by insert paths (gptel.el:1942 only moves it when tracking-marker is NIL).\"; echo \"2. Tool loop re-sends with SAME fsm (gptel--handle-wait re-calls curl-get-response with same fsm; gptel-send--handlers TRET-\u003eWAIT).\"; echo \"3. post-response hook fires once at DONE/ERRS/ABRT with position..tracking = whole conversation.\"; echo \"4. iar--cycle-log-append appends that whole region (iar-agent-cycle.el:101-130).\"; echo \"5. BONUS: two latent guard bugs (cross-response accumulation, output-runaway false-positive risk) + one strike-counting bug (mid-run ERRS start!=end) all trace to the same root and are FIXED by the same per-turn region fix. ===\""}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T19:06:16.966077047Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T19:06:17.034713825Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7957572884,"prompt_eval_count":149357,"prompt_eval_cached_count":143360,"eval_count":490}\n(5853de04addc53ba634db9ac6de6cf74 . 624)
