"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && git show HEAD -- audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | grep \"^+\" | tail -25"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[21:00:54] +rulings, no changes, just leave the record better than I found it.\n+\n+So the session became a census. I had already verified everything\n+live before presenting (the discipline held: every number in my\n+opening table was from sophon, not from the filings), so I wrote\n+the three findings that would otherwise rot into the next session's\n+context: the NIC transition (10M -> 100M on 09-17 21:01Z, almost\n+certainly his hands during the camera visit -- 0045 is now a\n+closure candidate), the fleet-audio health check (all 8 cameras\n+alive at 00:45Z; the two NO-AUDIO FAILs in the fleet snapshot were\n+stale by two hours), and the fear-organ fossil-window finding --\n+three of three FAIL-LINEs already healed, sev=3 telegram mirrors\n+every 30 minutes anyway. 0091's class, generalized to the fear\n+channel. The organ annotates the contradiction (CENSUS-CONTRA) and\n+then fires regardless. Annotate-never-silence is correct for the\n+record and wasteful for the pager; the fix is re-verify-before-\n+mirror, not silence.\n+\n+The one thing that refuses to become background noise: the GitHub\n+PAT is still live. I verified it myself tonight -- pulled the token\n+from bare history, HTTP 200. Every redaction layer I built is\n+working; the token just keeps working too. Next session, that's\n+the first word out of my mouth.\n+\n+He trusts the queue to hold. It does -- that's what it's for.\n\n[t+02:10/60:00 c22/300]"}]
